{"title":"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of the region enclosed by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph\" title=\"Graph\">graph</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/c/e2ce57d1aa4f2ba0d88bdffe754b1cf179b14809.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-60|+|y|=\\left|\\frac{x}{4}\\right|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"160\" height=\"34\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:1987_AIME-4.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/4/4e/1987_AIME-4.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"442\" height=\"362\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da61c635016c9cb19b665aef5d4225921056726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonnegative\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nonnegative\">nonnegative</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/23961d413021c629951e278b635481249452ce41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\frac{x}{4}\\right| \\ge |x - 60|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"109\" height=\"34\" />. Solving this gives us two equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93ad73dd6719af3451e2a12b356b7bcc47e5881b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{4} \\ge x - 60\\ \\mathrm{and} \\ -\\frac{x}{4} \\le x - 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"240\" height=\"33\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/b/30b5ab5f55d30587fcd50ce2484db5ee7315d8fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48 \\le x \\le 80$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Maximum\" title=\"Maximum\">maximum</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Minimum\" title=\"Minimum\">minimum</a> y value is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd21a6032c5c966e49928be55ffafd1f568c6445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x - 60| = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"18\" />, which is when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfc5a8f24764e16ec1b4fc73871ed11704a6b35f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 60$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/2/222e419e21b3af8b0d85a2f775ffdfa54155396d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\pm 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"65\" height=\"16\" />. Since the graph is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Symmetry\" title=\"Symmetry\">symmetric</a> about the y-axis, we just need <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Casework\" title=\"Casework\">casework</a> upon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/5/ef5be097dd3a8271309b4eff6d4314c4e8f77693.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{4} &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"47\" height=\"33\" />, so we break up the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/2/ee232229f7f00de473580641c3c2c7102275825f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x-60|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />:\n</p>\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/2/fb2ae3b42237b116d6bc438370dc423da35593c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 60 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841725622e3a36db9ad003e4f7264aa3e15a0d85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -\\frac{3}{4}x+60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa4ad1fb6694a5acd2913b6fee8db3b6d0f7fc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x - 60 &lt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f0871ebaf7b506fa85486e6e844b66005bb6d74f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{5}{4}x-60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>The area of the region enclosed by the graph is that of the quadrilateral defined by the points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22e1c38702db70b1e787482a4eff76d17bbee0e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(48,0),\\ (60,15),\\ (80,0), \\ (60,-15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"269\" height=\"18\" />. Breaking it up into triangles and solving or using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Shoelace_Theorem\" title=\"Shoelace Theorem\">Shoelace Theorem</a>, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/3/6f3156935b0d5f0d3d26747c4d2d150b5d3867cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}(80 - 48)(15) = \\boxed{480}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"203\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/6/da61c635016c9cb19b665aef5d4225921056726c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"18\" /> is the only present <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> \"term\" in this equation, we know that the area must be symmetrical about the x-axis.\n</p><p>We'll consider the area when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/3/cf32406671fc9a01b1982019404e3f981a0f56b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> and we only consider the portion enclosed with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Then, we'll double that area since the graph is symmetrical. \n</p><p>Now, let us remove the absolute values: \n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/8/3b8619a6902760a312273e00bffb6b2c9ff8fe47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/c/9cc25c068e2f60cf41e5d6f5a8bd93167756f711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x-60+y=0.25x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"151\" height=\"17\" />. This rearranges to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/3/75370fe32dee69706bbb57ef2b45ade07abc3fc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-0.75x+60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/4/d74788d23d565659cdf91f16ec3e2659b95e4279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0\\le x&lt;60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"16\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/b/41bd256b34c9fff865bf87aaf5ca4b3bb89b9398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60-x+y=0.25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a990582a7bf2987e2d0fa56e3b93cecf34cac961.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1.25x-60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/6/cd6ee81a7a535d87853e848c77654cc36104a75e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x&lt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff31c8f37190438c02a2b5a1b2ff82356dc5d9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60-x+y=-0.25x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"166\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca7debdae9c5a707460e43955c616d4e896b7ace.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0.75x-60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>By simple sketching, we see the shape that looks like the image in Solution 1 (graph it out and you'll see). We see that the partial area we seek in this part is the triangle with the vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7dee2555799a50507d327a32b46c7dd1d93d4055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(60,15)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46ad1c41651a311fa9c96432778fc015b0c10946.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(48,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/6/ea6ad3f0fa1afb6ff55b9f8670453e51f76fc31a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(80,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />. This triangle has an area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/5/345f59c386bd90fb155a046f26386a81b1235948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(80-48)*15*0.5=240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Simply double the area and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/7/a472d133f4ab89020583f7ca46f2adc11e0aaac9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{480}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> as our final answer.\n~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME\" title=\"1987 AIME\">1987 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016225910\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.039 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 260/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6446/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.608      1 -total\n 59.60%    7.514      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.67%    4.875      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with k